!+++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
1) Recommended environment for Olivia

   module reset
   module load NRIS/CPU
   module load GSL/2.8-intel-compilers-2024.2.0
   module load ESMF/8.8.0-intel-2024a-ParallelIO-2.6.5
   module load UDUNITS/2.2.28-GCCcore-13.3.0
   module load FFTW/3.3.10-GCC-13.3.0
   module load CMake/3.29.3-GCCcore-13.3.0

   execute the following line to get the environment (adjust the path if needed): 
   source ~/NERSC-HYCOM-CICE/environment/olivia_env.sh

2) Compiling hycom_all under NERSC-HYCOM-CICE/hycom/hycom_ALL/hycom_2.2.72_ALL

   # Define "setenv ARCH intelIFX" in Make_all.src
   csh Make_all.com

   !! NOT COMPLETE

        Netcdf routines are partly compiled right, 
        csh Make_ncdf.com

        but for someones are interested,
        
3) Compiling MSCPROGS under NERSC-HYCOM-CICE/hycom/MSCPROGS/src

       Go to NERSC-HYCOM-CICE/hycom/MSCPROGS/src/Make.Inc/
       execute:
          ln -s make.olivia.ifx make.inc
          cd ../
          gmake clean
          gmake all
          gmake install

4) Compiling hycom_cice under TP0a1.00/expt_01.0 (Untested)

   Use cluster selection for Olivia as the `hostname -d` method doesn't work

      compile_model.sh -c olivia -u ifx

   The added -c option sets SITE/cluster explicitly and bypasses hostname/domain 
   autodetection.

   This should select these build files which were prepared for Olivia:
      hycom/RELO/config/Linux.olivia.ifx_cice.V22
      hycom/RELO/config/Linux.olivia.ifx_cice.V23
      cice/Release-5.1/bld/Macros.Linux.olivia.ifx

   These are some of the issues when running `create_ref_case.sh` that I've found that is not fixed:
      - There is a module load at line 132 in `create_ref_case.sh`.
      - In bin/ice_climatology/extract_clim_iceh.sh there is a module load at line 87
        and 90. The equivalent modules on Olivia are not compatible with the compilation 
        environment modules.

5) prepare the python tools on Olivia

  NB: Adapt the $PYLIBSPATH variable in py-nhc-env-post.sh

  Make sure the `hpc-containerize` module is loaded:
      module load NRIS/CPU
      module load hpc-container-wrapper

  run `create_python_env.sh`.

  To load the python environment, add /path/to/NERSC-HYCOM-CICE/environment/py-nhc/py-nhc-env/bin 
  to $PATH.

